// THE MODEL REGISTRY: every kind of object the game draws, and whether what
// the player sees is a MODEL made in Blender (`make models`, committed in
// `pwa/models/`, the `blender-assets` skill) or GENERATED by the game's own
// code at run time. One row an asset: its ids, where each half lives and
// the switch that sends a modelled asset back to its code.
//
// A modelled asset keeps its code builder — the switch's other side, and
// what the model is judged against — so every row names one. The road, the
// terrain and its water, the sky and the weather, the dust, the spray, the
// tyre tracks and the snow's marks are surfaces and effects, not objects,
// and are not rows.
//
// `tests/model_registry_test.ts` holds it to the tree: the Blender rows'
// files are exactly the files the build packs (`modelFiles`), every path
// named here exists, and `docs/models.md` carries `renderModelRegistry()`
// (`make model-registry` rewrites it, and prettier pads its columns).
// DOM-free and three-free.

